---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---
<DocsLayout title="Development" activeSlug="development" description="Build, test, and contribute to PAS-Agent: Rust workspace layout, checks to run, and the Astro website.">
  <h1>Development</h1>

  <h2>Prerequisites</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Rust</strong>, 1.85 or later (Cargo is included)</li>
    <li><strong>Git</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Bun</strong>, only for the website</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Clone and Build</h2>
  <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/gfirik/pas-agent.git
cd pas-agent
cargo build</code></pre>

  <h2>Run Tests</h2>
  <pre><code>cargo test</code></pre>
  <p>
    Unit tests live next to the code in <code>pas-agent-core</code>. End-to-end tests that
    run the real binary live in <code>crates/pas-agent-cli/tests/</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Lint and Format</h2>
  <pre><code>cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo fmt --check</code></pre>

  <h2>Website</h2>
  <pre><code>cd website
bun install
bun run dev     # local dev server
bun run build   # static output in dist/</code></pre>

  <h2>Project Structure</h2>
  <pre><code>pas-agent/
├── Cargo.toml                    # Workspace root
├── crates/
│   ├── pas-agent-core/          # Core library
│   │   ├── Cargo.toml
│   │   └── src/
│   │       ├── lib.rs
│   │       ├── session.rs        # Session model
│   │       ├── storage.rs        # File persistence
│   │       ├── context.rs        # Context generation
│   │       └── git.rs            # Git state capture
│   └── pas-agent-cli/           # CLI binary
│       ├── Cargo.toml
│       ├── src/
│       │   └── main.rs
│       └── tests/
│           └── cli.rs            # End-to-end CLI tests
├── website/                      # Landing page + docs (Astro)
│   └── DESIGN.md                 # Website design system
├── .github/workflows/            # CI and release builds
├── AGENTS.md                     # Contributor rules (CLAUDE.md imports it)
└── CONTRIBUTING.md</code></pre>

  <h2>Contributing</h2>
  <p>
    PAS-Agent is open source and welcomes contributions. Before submitting
    a pull request:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Run <code>cargo test</code>: all tests must pass</li>
    <li>Run <code>cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings</code>: no warnings</li>
    <li>Run <code>cargo fmt</code>: code must be formatted</li>
    <li>Keep changes focused: one feature or fix per PR</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>License</h2>
  <p>
    PAS-Agent is licensed under the <strong>MIT License</strong>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
